aas (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Bluetooth audio under aas: drop-ins for bluez-alsa's bluealsa and
    bluealsa-aplay units run them only when aas is chosen, as the A2DP
    sink, playing into aas with the phone's volume on Master. Under
    PipeWire both are skipped and PipeWire's bluez5 stays the sink.

 -- HiFiBerry <info@hifiberry.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:51:53 +0000

aas (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First packaged release: the aas audio server and its command-line
    client, and the ALSA plugin as libasound2-plugin-aas.
  * hifiberry-audio-server switches a device between PipeWire and aas.
    The packages are installed disabled and change nothing until it is run.
  * aas-config writes /etc/aas/aas.toml from the HiFiBerry system info at
    every boot; /etc/aas/aas.local.toml is merged over it.

 -- HiFiBerry <info@hifiberry.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
